+**ornith-1.5-8bit** — 35.0 / 26.0 / 25.0 / 24.5. Run-2 is the only coherent
+per-channel, post-send design; the other three use global or per-run state.
+
+- *Good.* Run-2 verifies per-feed identity, first-run behavior, dry-run
+  non-consumption, failure isolation, and an additive `delivered` migration.
+  It is the only run whose state placement holds up under partial failure.
+- *Bad.* Run-1's global mark starves a failed or newly added channel. Run-3
+  crashes on an existing database and duplicates earlier successful channels
+  after a later failure; run-4 marks unmatched items and duplicates earlier
+  channel deliveries after a later failure.
+
+**ornith-1.5-4bit** — 30.0 / 29.5 / 24.0 / 20.0. Runs 2 and 4 improve to
+per-channel post-send ledgers; runs 1 and 3 do not.
+
+- *Good.* Runs 2 and 4 use canonical-link per-channel state, post-success
+  marking, and fixture-verified identity; run-2 adds tests and run-4's additive
+  ledger works on an old database.
+- *Bad.* Run-1 crashes during the legacy `items.key` migration. Run-3 uses
+  global state, consumes state in dry-run, and loses pre-send failures; runs 2
+  and 4 omit README-level first-run and operational guidance.
+
 **claude-sonnet-4.6-max** — 28.5 / 24.0 / 21.5 / 18.0. Identity improves run
 over run; state handling never does.
 
